WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.008
[opening theme music playing]

01:46.731 --> 01:49.025
[music fades]

01:49.109 --> 01:56.074
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

01:59.119 --> 02:01.121
[eerie music playing]

02:07.127 --> 02:09.129
[Morse code beeping]

02:17.929 --> 02:20.932
ALL TROOPS RETREAT

02:23.518 --> 02:24.352
[sighs]

02:26.896 --> 02:28.022
[foot stamps]

02:28.106 --> 02:29.858
Preparations for retreat
should be finished

02:29.941 --> 02:31.776
within the next 48 hours.

02:31.860 --> 02:35.363
All of our research records
and our documents are to return to Japan.

02:35.864 --> 02:39.784
That means anything that cannot be taken
should be completely incinerated.

02:39.868 --> 02:40.994
[officers] Yes, sir!

02:48.001 --> 02:49.085
[man] Sir, are we

02:50.170 --> 02:51.254
burning everything?

02:51.337 --> 02:53.047
Burn all of it. That's an order.

02:53.548 --> 02:55.717
Destroy all evidence
of us having been here.

02:56.342 --> 02:58.261
Nothing gets left behind. Not a thing.

02:58.928 --> 02:59.888
That is all.

03:03.057 --> 03:05.059
[unsettling music playing]

03:07.020 --> 03:09.147
- [man 1] Quickly! Let's go!
- [man 2] Destroy everything!

03:09.230 --> 03:11.524
[man 1] Quickly! Let's go!
Let's go! Let's go! Now!

03:13.067 --> 03:14.694
- [man 3] Quickly! Hurry!
- [man 4] Yes, sir!

03:14.777 --> 03:17.405
- [man 5] Don't leave any evidence!
- [man 6] We don't have time!

03:19.115 --> 03:21.117
[unsettling music continues]

03:23.244 --> 03:25.955
[gas masks hissing]

03:37.467 --> 03:39.469
[music intensifies]

03:48.436 --> 03:49.437
UNIT 731

03:58.655 --> 04:00.198
[breathing nervously]

04:01.658 --> 04:03.201
- It's been planted, sir.
- Over there!

04:03.284 --> 04:04.202
Okay!

04:15.046 --> 04:17.382
- The serums?
- We've secured 12 for you, sir.

04:17.465 --> 04:19.550
- And the Najin?
- We've secured a total of eight, sir.

04:19.634 --> 04:21.177
What about the other two items?

04:21.261 --> 04:23.554
We couldn't get any.
We ran out of time, sir.

04:31.562 --> 04:33.231
[loud bang]

04:34.857 --> 04:37.193
- [loud bang]
- Lt. Kato!

04:40.196 --> 04:42.532
[eerie music playing]

04:42.615 --> 04:44.117
[loud bang]

04:45.118 --> 04:47.829
[officer] There's not enough time!
We must hurry, sir!

04:48.871 --> 04:49.706
[loud bang]

04:51.124 --> 04:53.126
[unsettling music playing]

04:54.711 --> 04:55.962
[loud bang]

04:59.716 --> 05:00.883
[banging continues]

05:08.891 --> 05:10.310
[banging continues]

05:30.663 --> 05:31.539
[officer] Ready!

05:32.874 --> 05:34.375
[whimpering]

05:34.459 --> 05:35.960
- [officer] Fire!
- [screaming]

05:45.386 --> 05:46.220
[officer] Fire!

05:47.138 --> 05:48.848
[bullet casings rattling]

05:49.515 --> 05:50.433
[officer] Fire!

05:52.310 --> 05:53.603
[loud bang]

05:54.479 --> 05:55.813
[soldier 1] Hey, hurry up!

05:58.316 --> 05:59.317
Hurry! Let's go!

05:59.400 --> 06:00.777
[loud bang]

06:00.860 --> 06:01.819
[whimpering]

06:01.903 --> 06:04.322
Light it! What are you doing?
Hurry up! Light it!

06:04.405 --> 06:05.490
[grunts]

06:06.074 --> 06:08.076
[breathing heavily]

06:17.835 --> 06:19.837
[melancholy music playing]

06:44.654 --> 06:46.322
[soldier 1] Let's go. There's no time!

06:47.490 --> 06:50.868
- Are we flying?
- Sir, flying in a plane is too big a risk.

06:50.952 --> 06:52.161
We'll board a train at Harbin.

06:52.245 --> 06:54.497
You'll be transferred to Gyeongseong
from there.

06:54.580 --> 06:55.957
- Let's go.
- [soldier 2] Yes, sir!

07:09.637 --> 07:11.639
[tense music playing]

07:19.981 --> 07:21.983
[gasping, whimpering]

07:26.112 --> 07:28.114
[man screaming]

07:30.158 --> 07:32.160
[creature roaring]

07:39.292 --> 07:40.751
[music fades]

07:46.174 --> 07:49.552
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN GOOD AND EVIL

07:49.635 --> 07:52.180
EPISODE 1
NAJIN

07:53.681 --> 07:55.683
[train horn blares]

07:56.642 --> 07:58.644
[soothing music playing]

08:00.188 --> 08:02.023
LATE MARCH, 1945
GYEONGSEONG (OLD SEOUL)

08:02.106 --> 08:05.568
[man] Spring found its way to Gyeongseong
unusually quickly that year.

08:06.569 --> 08:08.279
[brakes squeal]

08:10.907 --> 08:12.825
[indistinct chattering]

08:31.886 --> 08:33.387
[tram bell ringing]

08:38.309 --> 08:42.146
- [boy 1] Get your papers here! Newspapers!
- [boy 2] Shoe shine! Shoe shine!

08:42.230 --> 08:44.482
- [boy 1] Papers! Newspapers here!
- [man 1] Hey, boy!

08:44.565 --> 08:45.983
[man 2] Get your paper!

08:46.067 --> 08:48.027
- Thank you.
- [man 2] Newspapers!

08:48.110 --> 08:50.613
- Boy, I'll take a newspaper.
- [boy 2] Shoe shine!

08:53.074 --> 08:53.950
One jeon, sir.

08:58.496 --> 09:00.456
Keep the change.
Go buy yourself some bread.

09:00.540 --> 09:03.626
[boy] Thank you, sir! May you be blessed.

09:07.797 --> 09:09.006
Tell you what.

09:10.049 --> 09:11.634
This is what's really happening here.

09:15.179 --> 09:16.264
Papers! Papers!

09:16.347 --> 09:18.349
JAPAN'S CRISIS!
LARGE-SCALE AIR RAIDS WRECK TOKYO

09:18.432 --> 09:20.393
So apparently,
all of the rumors were true.

09:21.602 --> 09:24.188
[man] After the bombing of Tokyo
on March 9th,

09:24.272 --> 09:26.774
a shadow of defeat loomed over Japan.

09:27.441 --> 09:32.446
Joseon waited in quiet anticipation
in the hopes that Japan might fall.

09:32.530 --> 09:33.447
However…

09:33.531 --> 09:35.908
[whistle blowing]

09:37.910 --> 09:40.413
The rebels are over here! Arrest them now!

09:41.330 --> 09:42.748
[people clamoring, shouting]

09:47.461 --> 09:48.921
[officer] Hey, don't move!

09:51.424 --> 09:52.842
[officer shouting]

09:52.925 --> 09:53.926
Come on. Let's go.

09:54.885 --> 09:56.095
[whistle blowing]

10:01.058 --> 10:02.435
- [man 1] Here.
- [man 2] What is it?

10:03.311 --> 10:04.478
[door slams]

10:05.563 --> 10:06.689
[man 3] Everyone, run!

10:06.772 --> 10:08.065
[all clamoring]

10:08.149 --> 10:09.817
[grunting]

10:21.662 --> 10:23.122
[screaming]

10:26.459 --> 10:28.002
[music fades]

10:29.211 --> 10:33.090
People of the peninsula, rise!
Your moment's here!

10:33.174 --> 10:36.218
Your opportunity
to die for His Majesty the Emperor!

10:36.302 --> 10:40.264
Join the unbeatable Imperial Army
and enter the shrine of Yasukuni!

10:40.348 --> 10:41.724
[men grunt]

10:44.018 --> 10:45.978
You may choose
to die in the torture chamber…

10:48.898 --> 10:50.650
or with honor in the Imperial Army.

10:54.195 --> 10:55.780
It's your choice.

10:57.948 --> 11:00.660
[man 1 sobs] Now what? What do I do?

11:02.787 --> 11:03.746
I can't.

11:03.829 --> 11:06.791
CONSCRIPTION FORM

11:06.874 --> 11:10.753
[man] They say that it is always darkest
before the dawn.

11:11.462 --> 11:14.548
- [electrical crackling]
- [groaning in pain]

11:18.552 --> 11:20.554
- [electrical crackling stops]
- [panting]

11:24.809 --> 11:25.935
Go on. Admit it.

11:26.018 --> 11:27.561
[panting]

11:28.688 --> 11:29.647
It wasn't me.

11:30.272 --> 11:32.858
Don't deny it. It'll make this harder.

11:33.442 --> 11:34.527
I'm telling you…

11:36.904 --> 11:39.115
I know nothing about what you're asking.

11:42.618 --> 11:45.162
- [electrical crackling]
- [groaning in pain]

11:49.041 --> 11:50.167
[man 2] Is he a rebel?

11:50.668 --> 11:53.295
- You really don't know who that man is?
- [man groaning in background]

11:53.379 --> 11:54.547
That's Jang Tae-sang.

11:55.673 --> 11:58.008
Jang Tae-sang? Who is he?

11:58.592 --> 12:00.803
He's the master
of the House of Golden Treasure.

12:01.303 --> 12:02.430
The House of Golden Treasure?

12:02.513 --> 12:03.889
[whimsical music playing]

12:03.973 --> 12:06.475
[man] That's right.
The House of Golden Treasure.

12:06.976 --> 12:10.312
Located in the Bonjeong district, with
the most valuable piece of real estate,

12:10.396 --> 12:12.898
it is, without a doubt,

12:12.982 --> 12:15.568
Gyeongseong's largest
and finest establishment.

12:15.651 --> 12:18.028
The great pawnshop.

12:20.698 --> 12:22.992
This is a Waltham watch.
They're famous, you know.

12:23.993 --> 12:25.119
I'll give you 450.

12:25.202 --> 12:26.245
[gasps]

12:26.996 --> 12:29.457
This here watch is valuable.
It's from America.

12:30.040 --> 12:31.375
Here's 450, then.

12:32.460 --> 12:33.961
[men chattering indistinctly]

12:34.044 --> 12:35.045
Please, sir.

12:35.129 --> 12:38.215
I just… I just lost my… my factory
to the Japanese.

12:38.299 --> 12:40.801
- And I'm losing my house too!
- Really? Oh.

12:40.885 --> 12:42.511
- I have an elderly mother.
- That so, um--

12:42.595 --> 12:44.054
And four children to feed, sir.

12:44.138 --> 12:46.474
- Do you wanna see us out on the street?
- Enough. Fine, then.

12:46.557 --> 12:47.391
[man] Sir, please!

12:47.475 --> 12:49.101
This is all you're getting, huh?

12:49.185 --> 12:52.438
Take it or leave it, okay?
Otherwise, you can forfeit it all.

12:52.521 --> 12:54.523
[whimsical music continues]

12:55.900 --> 12:57.067
Next person!

12:57.651 --> 13:00.821
[woman] These are my dowries,
so please take good care of them.

13:00.905 --> 13:03.824
No matter what,
I'll… I'll return for them.

13:03.908 --> 13:05.576
[employee] Fifteen won for all of it.

13:06.160 --> 13:08.370
And for the record,
I know this one's a fake.

13:08.454 --> 13:09.997
[man 2] This is a suit from Italy.

13:10.080 --> 13:11.874
I had the whole thing
custom-made from there.

13:11.957 --> 13:13.501
It's been worn. How about two won?

13:14.585 --> 13:15.753
It's real porcelain.

13:15.836 --> 13:17.838
I got it around three years ago,
and it wasn't cheap.

13:17.922 --> 13:19.965
Ah! You enjoy it, then.

13:21.091 --> 13:23.511
'Cause all it's good for is to piss in it.

13:25.471 --> 13:26.680
What an idiot.

13:28.057 --> 13:29.725
- [elevator bell dings]
- [music stops]

13:29.809 --> 13:31.811
[humming]

13:44.406 --> 13:45.366
[chuckles]

13:54.124 --> 13:56.210
- What is it?
- [sighs] Give it here.

14:00.923 --> 14:03.050
[chuckles]

14:08.597 --> 14:10.808
You steal one more item from this company,

14:11.433 --> 14:13.936
I'll cut off your fingers
before you can even blink, you got it?

14:14.019 --> 14:17.773
Ah, you don't have to be so dramatic.
I was playing around, that's all.

14:20.025 --> 14:22.027
[pensive music playing]

14:36.917 --> 14:37.793
[grunts]

14:41.046 --> 14:43.048
[mystical music playing]

15:03.277 --> 15:04.153
[man] Hmm?

15:04.778 --> 15:06.530
A Waltham. That's a rare find.

15:07.031 --> 15:09.575
[sighs] Four won would have been plenty.

15:10.159 --> 15:12.286
He gave the guy five and a half for it.

15:12.369 --> 15:13.871
Mr. Gu always does this.

15:13.954 --> 15:16.749
Giving money away so generously
as if it belongs to him.

15:16.832 --> 15:18.500
[man] This is quality leather.

15:19.418 --> 15:20.419
It was worth it.

15:20.920 --> 15:23.255
That Beom-o boy is a thief.
I'm just letting you know.

15:23.339 --> 15:25.215
The brat's completely hopeless.

15:25.299 --> 15:27.384
He always pockets things
every chance he gets.

15:27.468 --> 15:30.304
The teacup set
and china plates for Lady Maeda?

15:30.387 --> 15:31.597
Is that order ready yet?

15:32.765 --> 15:33.682
[woman] Be careful.

15:33.766 --> 15:37.186
If you get too close to the fire,
then you just might get burned, hmm?

15:37.269 --> 15:40.147
Her husband is Ishikawa,
and her father is General Maeda.

15:40.230 --> 15:42.191
I'm just, uh, keeping us afloat here

15:42.274 --> 15:44.652
by keeping the powerful
as happy as possible.

15:45.361 --> 15:47.488
It's only natural
that I do business with them, yes?

15:49.365 --> 15:51.408
You need to be careful. They're Japanese.

15:51.492 --> 15:52.785
I'm Jang Tae-sang.

15:53.535 --> 15:54.453
Okay?

15:55.371 --> 15:57.873
It'll all work out. [chuckles]

15:57.957 --> 16:00.292
- That's right. I am Jang Tae-sang.
- [swing music playing]

16:01.126 --> 16:04.630
A man of many means
and an icon for self-made men.

16:07.758 --> 16:10.219
- [woman 1 gasps] It's Master Jang!
- [woman 2] Oh my goodness!

16:10.302 --> 16:11.470
[woman 3] Oh!

16:12.096 --> 16:13.222
- Hello, everyone.
- Hello, sir.

16:13.305 --> 16:14.306
Master Jang!

16:14.390 --> 16:16.558
- Control yourselves.
- Okay, we will.

16:16.642 --> 16:18.686
[photographer] One, two! Good! One more!

16:18.769 --> 16:20.229
How about a different pose, ladies?

16:22.064 --> 16:23.399
[pool balls rattle]

16:23.482 --> 16:25.025
[indistinct chattering]

16:31.448 --> 16:32.616
[woman] Master Jang!

16:33.200 --> 16:35.411
[Tae-sang] I had nothing to fear.
Nothing stood in my way.

16:35.494 --> 16:37.621
I was the master
of the House of Golden Treasure.

16:37.705 --> 16:39.999
I could get anything
and everything I wanted.

16:40.082 --> 16:41.667
A toast! To everyone.

16:41.750 --> 16:43.502
[all] Cheers!

16:44.253 --> 16:46.880
[Tae-sang] I am
the one and only Jang Tae-sang.

16:48.173 --> 16:49.008
So then…

16:50.300 --> 16:51.635
[music fades]

16:52.636 --> 16:54.179
[Tae-sang coughing]

16:56.473 --> 16:58.308
[gasps]

17:00.102 --> 17:02.730
…how did I end up in this horrible mess?

17:03.355 --> 17:06.150
[officer 1] He must have secretly funded
the independence movement.

17:06.233 --> 17:07.401
[officer 2] Wrong.

17:07.484 --> 17:09.445
Then what did he do? Was he a spy?

17:09.945 --> 17:10.779
Nope.

17:14.867 --> 17:15.951
It was an affair.

17:17.119 --> 17:18.203
An affair?

17:20.289 --> 17:23.876
You met my wife at a teahouse
about a month ago. Why was that?

17:24.960 --> 17:27.713
Lady Maeda wanted baekja teacups

17:27.796 --> 17:30.758
and china lacquered plates
inlaid with mother-of-pearl.

17:30.841 --> 17:32.760
And what about at the museum last week?

17:32.843 --> 17:35.471
I went to tell her the baekja teacups
and plates that she wanted

17:35.554 --> 17:37.973
were nearly impossible to find for her.

17:38.057 --> 17:40.142
The message you sent her
three days ago, what was it?

17:40.225 --> 17:44.229
I managed to find exactly
what she was asking me for.

17:45.022 --> 17:46.440
I wanted to tell her about my luck.

17:46.523 --> 17:48.692
And yesterday, you came
all the way to my house for…

17:48.776 --> 17:50.986
To deliver it all in person, seeing as…

17:52.988 --> 17:54.281
it took me so long to get it.

17:54.907 --> 17:56.283
[officer] Don't play games!

17:56.992 --> 17:59.620
- You pathetic little maggot!
- [grunting]

17:59.703 --> 18:00.746
You Josenjing lowlife!

18:00.829 --> 18:03.165
How dare you even think
of going after my wife,

18:03.248 --> 18:04.833
you little bastard, huh?

18:04.917 --> 18:06.919
[panting]

18:07.419 --> 18:10.214
Commissioner, seems that, uh,

18:11.090 --> 18:13.550
we have ourselves
a little misunderstanding.

18:14.259 --> 18:15.094
[grunts]

18:15.177 --> 18:17.721
That's enough bullshit.
I wanna know what's going on here.

18:18.263 --> 18:21.850
Say it. You better tell me exactly
what it is you're doing with my wife.

18:21.934 --> 18:23.102
Tell me, you bastard, huh?

18:23.977 --> 18:25.979
[laughing]

18:28.357 --> 18:30.150
Ah, I guess you are crazy.

18:30.234 --> 18:31.110
Huh?

18:32.152 --> 18:34.947
Crazy in love
with your wife, Commissioner.

18:35.656 --> 18:39.409
Don't tell me that you're
seriously suspicious of her.

18:39.493 --> 18:40.327
[grunts]

18:40.410 --> 18:44.414
Lady Maeda? Who carries such respect
and honor in her community?

18:44.498 --> 18:47.543
I gotta say, this is a… a major affront

18:47.626 --> 18:49.461
to a woman
who is incredibly pure of heart.

18:49.545 --> 18:50.921
What do you mean?

18:51.004 --> 18:54.049
What would you do
if Lady Maeda were to learn of this,

18:55.509 --> 18:58.470
about you openly
doubting her loyalty like this?

18:59.179 --> 19:00.013
You get it now?

19:02.975 --> 19:05.185
- [wind chime dings]
- [soothing music playing]

19:08.647 --> 19:10.440
[liquid pouring]

19:11.233 --> 19:12.276
[music fades]

19:14.444 --> 19:16.446
[pensive music playing]

19:27.666 --> 19:29.042
[music fades]

19:30.586 --> 19:31.795
[Tae-sang sighs]

19:37.593 --> 19:41.680
Okay, how about we move on
to the matter at hand?

19:42.723 --> 19:45.225
Let's hear
what you really want from me, huh?

19:49.688 --> 19:51.273
[officer] This girl has gone missing.

19:52.149 --> 19:53.442
[gentle music playing]

19:53.525 --> 19:56.528
It's been about a week,
and we still can't find her.

20:00.532 --> 20:02.326
I've never done a missing persons case.

20:03.911 --> 20:05.704
Well, I'm sure the police could help.

20:05.787 --> 20:07.998
Aren't you
the information king of Gyeongseong?

20:08.707 --> 20:10.125
I'm flattered. I really am.

20:10.209 --> 20:12.085
It's been said that if you want anything,

20:12.169 --> 20:14.379
the best person to go through
is Jang Tae-sang,

20:14.463 --> 20:17.299
whether to find a person
or even if you need some money.

20:18.550 --> 20:19.384
Is that right?

20:19.468 --> 20:22.304
I specialize in hunting people
who don't pay me back,

20:23.805 --> 20:25.557
not finding lost mistresses.

20:30.687 --> 20:32.522
You'll do whatever I ask you to.

20:33.941 --> 20:35.984
Find out why she disappeared,
where she went,

20:36.068 --> 20:38.570
and does she have another lover,
and if so, who is it?

20:38.654 --> 20:41.073
And why don't you find the man, too,
while you're at it?

20:42.282 --> 20:43.533
Find her.

20:44.076 --> 20:46.370
And if you don't bring in
this woman of mine…

20:47.704 --> 20:48.580
You'll kill me?

20:52.084 --> 20:56.213
No, but you will lose everything
that you hold close and dear to you.

20:57.547 --> 21:00.175
The house that you own,
real estate, cash, cars,

21:00.259 --> 21:03.136
the House of Golden Treasure you built
will be taken away.

21:03.220 --> 21:04.263
It'll be gone!

21:05.681 --> 21:06.974
You'll lose it all.

21:07.057 --> 21:08.392
And as for you?

21:09.935 --> 21:11.979
Oh, you will be sent away to war.

21:25.409 --> 21:26.493
[officer sighs]

21:26.994 --> 21:28.996
[tense music playing]

21:34.293 --> 21:36.253
So then how much time do I have?

21:39.214 --> 21:42.384
Till the flowers fall from the trees.

21:43.719 --> 21:45.929
[scoffs]

21:49.933 --> 21:50.976
All right, then.

21:53.770 --> 21:54.980
Glad to help out.

22:07.909 --> 22:09.328
[door opens]

22:09.411 --> 22:10.579
[music fades]

22:11.079 --> 22:12.080
[man] Master Jang.

22:25.010 --> 22:27.012
[door opening]

22:29.639 --> 22:30.474
[sighs]

22:30.557 --> 22:32.434
[woman] What happened? What's the matter?

22:34.686 --> 22:37.939
Goodness! What happened?
Who did this to your face?

22:38.440 --> 22:39.274
[sighs]

22:39.816 --> 22:44.112
I need to know. How much cash
do we have available right now?

22:45.447 --> 22:46.490
What's it for?

22:49.201 --> 22:51.286
If I put my Bukchon house and properties

22:51.912 --> 22:54.289
and the House of Golden Treasure
up for sale,

22:54.915 --> 22:57.042
how fast would everything sell, you think?

22:58.251 --> 23:00.253
[indistinct chattering]

23:03.256 --> 23:04.758
Is a month enough time for us?

23:06.551 --> 23:10.013
What'd you do this time around, huh?
What kind of trouble are we in?

23:10.097 --> 23:12.099
[footsteps approaching]

23:18.271 --> 23:19.439
It seems like

23:20.732 --> 23:21.650
all my fortune…

23:24.528 --> 23:26.321
and luck has finally dried up.

23:26.822 --> 23:28.824
- [cheerful music playing]
- [chuckles]

23:32.869 --> 23:34.496
[woman] Come on over, sir.

23:34.579 --> 23:36.081
[indistinct chattering]

23:38.166 --> 23:40.585
He really knows how
to work those scissors, doesn't he?

23:41.920 --> 23:43.839
- [woman 2] Right.
- [woman 3] How are you, sir?

23:44.714 --> 23:45.882
Just wait here, all right?

23:45.966 --> 23:49.094
[indistinct chattering]

23:49.177 --> 23:51.179
[man] Goodness, it's wonderful.

23:51.721 --> 23:54.349
- [woman 2] Yes, he's great at it.
- [man] Yes.

23:57.477 --> 23:58.728
[man] Excuse me, miss?

24:00.063 --> 24:02.023
Sorry, sir, we haven't opened yet.

24:06.778 --> 24:08.738
I'm looking for someone. He's Japanese.

24:10.365 --> 24:13.368
I heard he's in Gyeongseong.
He's a guy in his mid-thirties.

24:13.452 --> 24:16.079
His name is Sachimoto.
He's a regular at this place.

24:17.622 --> 24:20.083
I've been told he was a painter
and a very good one.

24:20.167 --> 24:21.501
Sachimoto.

24:21.585 --> 24:23.837
I know two different men called that.

24:24.880 --> 24:27.382
But they were both soldiers,
not painters. Sorry.

24:29.134 --> 24:31.303
Well, I was told he was a regular here.

24:31.386 --> 24:32.554
Is that so?

24:33.138 --> 24:35.849
Well, I've been working
at the Moonlight Bar for half a year,

24:35.932 --> 24:37.726
and I've never met your Sachimoto.

24:38.894 --> 24:40.270
Okay, thanks for your time.

24:42.022 --> 24:44.524
[woman] Why don't you try
the House of Golden Treasure?

24:45.734 --> 24:49.154
Ask for Jang Tae-sang.
He's the one in charge there.

24:49.863 --> 24:52.157
If you ever need information,
he's full of it.

24:52.240 --> 24:54.159
In fact, nothing slips past the guy,

24:54.826 --> 24:58.413
whether it is a person,
a property, or money.

24:59.247 --> 25:01.791
He's called
the "information king" of Gyeongseong.

25:02.918 --> 25:03.752
What was that?

25:03.835 --> 25:06.796
I was asking if the, uh,
the motorcycle out there's for sale.

25:08.465 --> 25:10.050
[man] Oh, that thing?

25:11.134 --> 25:13.887
It doesn't run.
The engine's busted. Sorry.

25:13.970 --> 25:16.723
I'll take it anyway.
How much do you want for it?

25:16.806 --> 25:18.391
[intriguing music playing]

25:19.309 --> 25:22.604
[man] From the looks of you,
I'm guessing you're from Manchuria.

25:22.687 --> 25:24.189
- Am I right?
- 200 won?

25:24.272 --> 25:27.484
Hey, it comes with a sidecar, huh?

25:27.567 --> 25:29.194
I'll give it to you for 300.

25:29.277 --> 25:30.987
You just said the engine's busted.

25:31.947 --> 25:34.824
If you keep leaving it out there,
it'll be worthless junk.

25:34.908 --> 25:37.494
If you throw a diamond into the trash,
it's still a diamond.

25:37.577 --> 25:39.454
I'll give you the motorcycle for 300.

25:42.958 --> 25:43.917
[clears throat]

25:45.252 --> 25:46.211
280.

25:46.753 --> 25:49.214
Um, that's my best offer, hmm?

25:51.216 --> 25:53.134
- That's your best offer?
- Yes.

26:04.854 --> 26:06.189
[intriguing music continues]

26:08.024 --> 26:09.067
[items clattering]

26:10.193 --> 26:11.611
[sighs]

26:13.530 --> 26:16.074
I'll give you 250
including this stuff here.

26:17.284 --> 26:18.535
And that's my best offer.

26:18.618 --> 26:20.453
I don't take Chinese money, you know?

26:20.537 --> 26:22.539
[rhythmic drums playing]

26:30.922 --> 26:32.924
[music intensifies]

26:50.108 --> 26:51.318
- [man laughs]
- [music stops]

26:51.401 --> 26:53.945
That woman's going to be disappointed.
Look at this.

26:54.696 --> 26:57.532
My goodness.
I said it was busted, didn't I?

26:57.616 --> 27:00.744
That motorcycle has been outside
for three years through the rainstorms,

27:00.827 --> 27:02.495
the blizzards, the hail, everything.

27:02.579 --> 27:04.581
She's not getting
that thing running, nope.

27:04.664 --> 27:07.167
- [motorcycle engine revving]
- Hmm?

27:17.510 --> 27:20.764
[man claps] Forget it, all right?
There's no need to worry so much.

27:20.847 --> 27:22.432
Hey, what's with the look on your face?

27:22.515 --> 27:26.770
Look, you're the great Master Jang!
The information king of Gyeongseong!

27:26.853 --> 27:29.939
So just reach out to all your sources,
and she'll be found in no time, huh?

27:30.023 --> 27:32.442
I mean, it's the same Myeong-ja
we always see, Mrs. Nawol.

27:32.525 --> 27:34.861
She probably went off
and eloped with some other guy.

27:34.944 --> 27:37.864
What man in Gyeongseong
would be that stupid

27:38.490 --> 27:40.617
to go and elope with Ishikawa's side girl?

27:43.203 --> 27:45.580
Wait, could this be another one
of the missing women cases

27:45.664 --> 27:47.624
that's been going on recently?

27:48.458 --> 27:51.336
Everyone, including the town over,
has been talking about it.

27:51.836 --> 27:54.172
Women all over Joseon
have been disappearing, Master Jang.

27:54.756 --> 27:56.549
The rumors about it are horrible.

27:56.633 --> 27:58.677
What if this is
what happened to Myeong-ja?

27:59.260 --> 28:02.847
Oh no. This is really bad.
Now what? What do we do?

28:06.768 --> 28:07.686
All right.

28:08.812 --> 28:11.064
You must sell everything we have
in the vault, Master Jang,

28:11.147 --> 28:12.732
and then leave Joseon for good, huh?

28:12.816 --> 28:15.276
Ah yes, I got a really good friend
who lives in Osaka, and, um--

28:15.360 --> 28:17.737
You're being stupid, Mr. Gu! Just stop it!

28:17.821 --> 28:20.657
Let me voice my opinions
for once, Mrs. Nawol, huh?

28:20.740 --> 28:22.492
Why do you need
to shoot me down all the time?

28:22.575 --> 28:24.327
Why do you always treat me like this?
Tell me!

28:24.411 --> 28:27.330
Because most of what you have to say
usually doesn't make sense.

28:27.414 --> 28:29.457
Just so you know,
I do think before I speak.

28:29.541 --> 28:31.084
All I'm doing is trying to help, okay?

28:31.793 --> 28:35.922
Let's say Master Jang tries to sell.
Think about what would happen then.

28:36.506 --> 28:39.759
Rumors would begin to spread like wildfire
all over Gyeongseong.

28:39.843 --> 28:42.721
Who cares about stupid rumors?
Why would that be so horrible for us?

28:42.804 --> 28:44.806
Ishikawa will hear he's selling

28:45.557 --> 28:47.308
and send over all the policemen

28:48.476 --> 28:49.769
to take down Master Jang.

28:53.523 --> 28:54.524
Apologies to you.

28:55.942 --> 28:57.318
I did not think it through.

29:02.907 --> 29:04.659
[unsettling music playing]

29:16.463 --> 29:18.339
It does seem Ishikawa's got his eye on me.

29:19.257 --> 29:21.134
- Mr. Gu.
- Yes, Master Jang?

29:21.217 --> 29:22.969
Go and contact every informant of mine.

29:23.052 --> 29:25.972
See if anyone has any leads
regarding Myeong-Ja's disappearance.

29:26.473 --> 29:29.225
Do not leave any chair or table unturned.
We must find where she is.

29:29.309 --> 29:32.061
I understand. I think that's a great idea.

29:32.896 --> 29:34.856
Let's do everything possible, Mrs. Nawol.

29:36.649 --> 29:37.734
And you, Beom-o,

29:38.526 --> 29:40.278
send word to Master Jun-taek.

29:40.945 --> 29:42.238
[Mrs. Nawol] Why Master Jun-taek?

29:42.864 --> 29:44.407
He's the only man in all of Gyeongseong

29:44.491 --> 29:47.452
who's bold enough
to meddle with Ishikawa's mistress.

29:48.328 --> 29:50.663
- Let him know that I wanna see him.
- Yes, sir.

29:51.831 --> 29:53.041
And, Mrs. Nawol,

29:53.124 --> 29:56.920
the most expensive items in our collection
need to get sold as soon as possible.

29:57.003 --> 29:59.547
Discretion and privacy is
of great importance to us.

29:59.631 --> 30:01.424
Ishikawa will be watching our every move,

30:01.508 --> 30:03.593
so we will need
to watch our backs from now on.

30:04.803 --> 30:08.264
And please look into any ships departing
within the next month or sooner.

30:08.765 --> 30:09.891
If things get worse,

30:11.643 --> 30:13.812
we may all
have to leave Gyeongseong for good.

30:15.313 --> 30:16.606
[Mrs. Nawol] Yes, Master Jang.

30:20.276 --> 30:22.695
[unsettling music playing]

30:41.047 --> 30:43.466
It looks like
the information king of Gyeongseong

30:44.175 --> 30:46.261
has a lot of people
watching him for some reason.

30:58.940 --> 31:00.942
[tram bell ringing in distance]

31:05.822 --> 31:06.656
[door closing]

31:08.283 --> 31:10.493
[man] Master Jang is on the move,
Commissioner Ishikawa.

31:10.577 --> 31:12.495
All of his employees have been sent

31:12.579 --> 31:15.748
to look for any leads
regarding Miss Akiko's whereabouts, sir.

31:17.417 --> 31:18.376
All right, then.

31:19.377 --> 31:20.545
That's all.

31:20.628 --> 31:21.880
[man] I'll be going, sir.

31:27.010 --> 31:29.345
[breathes deeply]

31:34.642 --> 31:36.644
[sentimental music playing]

31:41.691 --> 31:44.360
[woman] I think that I'm pregnant.

31:47.739 --> 31:48.573
Pregnant?

31:49.532 --> 31:50.617
Yes.

31:51.200 --> 31:52.702
And the child is yours.

31:55.955 --> 31:56.873
[chuckles]

31:57.457 --> 31:58.541
[chuckles]

31:59.292 --> 32:00.919
- [knocking at door]
- [door opens]

32:01.794 --> 32:02.962
[door closes]

32:04.339 --> 32:06.132
[woman] You have a message
from your residence.

32:06.215 --> 32:08.843
They wish to know when you'll be
going home tonight, Mr. Ishikawa.

32:08.927 --> 32:10.637
I have a new case to work on,

32:11.763 --> 32:13.097
so I'll be home late.

32:13.890 --> 32:16.601
- Very late.
- Yes, sir. Understood.

32:17.477 --> 32:19.479
[footsteps departing]

32:23.691 --> 32:24.567
[woman] Yes.

32:25.652 --> 32:26.569
I see.

32:27.320 --> 32:29.447
No. Yes.

32:30.823 --> 32:31.741
Goodbye.

32:38.414 --> 32:40.416
[unsettling music playing]

32:41.334 --> 32:43.336
[footsteps approaching]

32:43.419 --> 32:45.588
- [loud clatter]
- [man] Get up! All of you!

32:45.672 --> 32:47.757
- To your positions!
- [loud clatter]

32:49.634 --> 32:52.053
- [man] Hurry up! Move your asses!
- [loud clatter]

32:57.308 --> 33:00.395
- Do you know what's happening right now?
- Do not make a sound.

33:00.895 --> 33:02.105
And keep your head down.

33:02.939 --> 33:03.815
What?

33:04.440 --> 33:06.442
[unsettling music continues]

33:09.737 --> 33:10.989
[door opens]

33:13.658 --> 33:16.327
[door closes]

33:25.336 --> 33:26.963
Will two be enough, you think?

33:27.505 --> 33:29.966
[officer] Yes,
two will be enough for now, sir.

33:31.426 --> 33:33.428
[ominous music playing]

33:40.018 --> 33:40.977
[officer] That one.

33:41.686 --> 33:43.354
- [doctor] Take her out.
- [soldier] Yes, sir.

33:47.567 --> 33:51.320
[woman 1] Please don't kill me. No!
I don't wanna die. Please don't kill me!

33:54.032 --> 33:55.950
[woman 1 sobbing]

33:56.034 --> 33:58.077
- [officer] Tell me about that one.
- [woman 1 sobs]

33:58.161 --> 34:02.040
[doctor] Ah, we brought her
from Seodaemun Prison a while ago,

34:02.874 --> 34:04.584
but her condition is a bit…

34:06.002 --> 34:07.128
[Kato] Let me see.

34:08.129 --> 34:09.964
- [doctor] Take her out.
- [soldier 2] Yes, sir.

34:13.092 --> 34:15.094
[unsettling music playing]

34:18.014 --> 34:20.016
- [loud clattering]
- [gasps]

34:27.065 --> 34:29.275
[breathing nervously]

34:39.535 --> 34:41.954
[woman 1] Don't kill me.
Don't kill me, please.

34:42.455 --> 34:44.874
- [soldier 3] Keep your head down.
- [woman 1] I don't wanna die.

34:44.957 --> 34:47.627
- [officer] What shall we do, sir?
- [woman 1] Please don't kill me.

34:49.003 --> 34:50.296
[sobs]

34:52.632 --> 34:54.092
[woman 1 sobs] Please don't kill me.

34:59.597 --> 35:01.182
I think these two will do.

35:01.682 --> 35:04.310
[woman 1 sobs] Please don't kill me.

35:05.019 --> 35:09.148
Please don't kill me! Oh, please!

35:09.232 --> 35:10.525
Have mercy on me.

35:11.567 --> 35:13.152
[woman 1] Please don't kill me!

35:13.236 --> 35:15.947
- Please don't kill me!
- [sobs]

35:18.533 --> 35:19.867
[sobs]

35:21.035 --> 35:23.079
[woman 1 sobs] Please don't kill me!

35:24.038 --> 35:25.957
[woman 1 crying]

35:26.040 --> 35:28.709
[door locks clanking]

35:28.793 --> 35:31.129
[sobs] Please let me go, sir.

35:31.212 --> 35:33.089
[unsettling music continues]

35:38.010 --> 35:39.637
[music fades]

35:39.720 --> 35:41.013
[woman 1 sobs]

36:01.617 --> 36:02.493
[sniffles]

36:29.395 --> 36:31.147
[sniffles, retches]

36:33.858 --> 36:35.443
[slurping]

36:38.905 --> 36:40.907
[unsettling music playing]

36:42.867 --> 36:44.076
[slurping]

37:00.927 --> 37:02.762
[unsettling music intensifies]

37:05.890 --> 37:07.808
[high-pitched shrill]

37:11.520 --> 37:13.898
[door opens, closes]

37:35.253 --> 37:36.754
- [screams]
- [gasps]

37:36.837 --> 37:38.839
[whimsical music playing]

37:43.719 --> 37:44.553
Yes, what is it?

37:44.637 --> 37:47.765
You think I can get a ride to Bukchon?
I have a meeting to attend tonight.

37:48.432 --> 37:49.517
But, um, what?

37:50.226 --> 37:51.769
How about I sit over there?

37:52.520 --> 37:54.689
You must be bored
from spying on me all day.

37:54.772 --> 37:55.898
You've been here a long time.

37:55.982 --> 37:57.984
I'm sure you wouldn't mind
a little break, would you?

37:58.484 --> 38:01.654
Isn't this better than having to tail me,
which is what you were about to do?

38:02.196 --> 38:05.199
[scoffs] Seriously?
Hey, wait. What are you--

38:05.283 --> 38:07.034
To Bukchon. Let's go, huh?

38:09.954 --> 38:10.997
[sighs]

38:12.456 --> 38:14.333
[Tae-sang] Come on, we don't have all day.

38:18.504 --> 38:20.506
[whimsical music continues]

38:29.181 --> 38:31.058
- [music fades]
- [liquid pouring]

38:31.142 --> 38:33.269
[man] My my, trying to empty out
the secret vault

38:33.352 --> 38:35.271
at the House of Golden Treasure?

38:35.354 --> 38:36.814
My goodness.

38:36.897 --> 38:39.942
Every single item listed
is very high quality. I promise you that.

38:40.026 --> 38:43.738
Of course it is. I wouldn't expect
anything less from you or Master Jang.

38:45.740 --> 38:48.200
Do you think you can
get this done for us in ten days?

38:48.284 --> 38:50.536
Ten days? Ah, that's a bit tight.

38:53.789 --> 38:57.835
Why the rush? Did something bad happen?
It's unlike you to do this.

38:57.918 --> 38:59.003
What is it, huh?

38:59.086 --> 39:02.131
Is Master Jang really leaving Gyeongseong
this time around?

39:02.840 --> 39:05.343
There are a lot of rumors
spreading throughout the town.

39:05.426 --> 39:08.262
Something about Master Jang
being in some kind of difficult situation

39:08.346 --> 39:09.680
because of Ishikawa.

39:09.764 --> 39:13.017
Shut your mouth now,
or I would be happy to do it for you.

39:15.353 --> 39:16.854
Look, I just…

39:16.937 --> 39:19.982
I mentioned it 'cause I heard
some sleuths are in town right now.

39:20.066 --> 39:22.651
I thought they could be
of great use to Master Jang.

39:23.861 --> 39:24.695
"Sleuths"?

39:24.779 --> 39:26.072
Yes, sleuths.

39:26.155 --> 39:27.907
They're experts
in locating missing people.

39:27.990 --> 39:29.367
It's what they do.

39:29.450 --> 39:32.536
In Manchuria,
they refer to these people as sleuths.

39:33.245 --> 39:34.163
Tell me more.

39:34.246 --> 39:37.124
Okay, so my friend's
cousin's brother's daughter

39:37.208 --> 39:40.461
went on a walk during the Dano Festival,
then went missing for three years.

39:40.544 --> 39:42.254
So guess what these guys did next?

39:42.922 --> 39:45.549
They pursued her all over China
and brought her back.

39:45.633 --> 39:48.636
She was kidnapped to be a comfort woman,
and they found her.

39:48.719 --> 39:50.304
They went all the way to China, you said?

39:50.388 --> 39:52.181
Oh yes. They went all over the map,

39:52.264 --> 39:55.559
including the west region,
Manchuria, and all around the border.

39:55.643 --> 39:56.644
They found everyone.

39:56.727 --> 39:58.687
And if they were dead,
they brought back the bones.

39:59.271 --> 40:00.147
I see.

40:02.817 --> 40:04.693
And is it possible to meet these people?

40:04.777 --> 40:07.238
[intriguing music playing]

40:09.824 --> 40:12.284
[tram bell ringing]

40:27.383 --> 40:28.926
[music stops]

40:29.009 --> 40:31.887
Ah, thanks for the ride.
I was very comfortable.

40:32.888 --> 40:34.223
[sighs]

40:38.936 --> 40:40.020
Uh-- Huh?

40:40.104 --> 40:42.523
- What are you doing? Stop. Come on!
- Oh. Don't be silly!

40:42.606 --> 40:44.650
Hey, go buy yourself dinner.

40:45.860 --> 40:49.447
I won't tell Ishikawa anything, okay?
You've earned it, hmm?

40:54.743 --> 40:55.619
Wait.

41:00.291 --> 41:01.125
What the…

41:04.879 --> 41:06.881
[pensive music playing]

41:15.848 --> 41:19.351
Hello, and welcome back.
And how many people in your party tonight?

41:19.435 --> 41:21.187
No, I'm not here to eat.

41:21.270 --> 41:23.981
I just need passage
through your establishment, please.

41:24.064 --> 41:25.983
I understand. This way, Master Jang.

41:47.046 --> 41:48.088
Okay.

41:50.216 --> 41:53.177
IDIOT

41:56.472 --> 41:58.474
[unsettling music playing]

42:37.346 --> 42:40.391
[Tae-sang] Who are you?
Why are you following me?

42:44.436 --> 42:46.897
You don't look like
one of Ishikawa's underlings.

42:47.898 --> 42:49.108
Who sent you here?

42:49.191 --> 42:51.110
Tell me who you work for,
and I'll let you go.

42:53.529 --> 42:55.030
Are you the one they call Master Jang?

42:55.114 --> 42:57.950
It's bad manners to answer a question
with another question.

42:58.867 --> 42:59.702
And also…

43:02.413 --> 43:05.040
why are you carrying
such a dangerous thing so brazenly.

43:56.175 --> 43:58.385
[gentle music playing]

44:30.709 --> 44:32.211
[music fades]

44:38.300 --> 44:39.385
Are you here to kill me?

44:39.968 --> 44:44.264
I wasn't going to kill you at all,
but now… I'm thinking about it.

44:44.348 --> 44:45.265
I am rather tempted.

44:46.684 --> 44:47.810
If you're not gonna kill me,

44:47.893 --> 44:50.771
then would you kindly lower your weapon
and talk to me?

44:50.854 --> 44:53.273
Why don't you be an example
and lower your weapon first?

44:53.357 --> 44:55.150
All right, then. I'll do that.

44:56.151 --> 44:59.071
On the count of three,
let's both lower our weapons.

44:59.154 --> 45:00.155
How about that?

45:00.823 --> 45:01.657
All right?

45:02.366 --> 45:03.200
One,

45:04.618 --> 45:05.452
two…

45:07.788 --> 45:08.872
and three.

45:10.666 --> 45:12.668
[breathes deeply]

45:13.293 --> 45:15.379
You don't trust me, do you now?

45:15.462 --> 45:17.172
I could say the same for you.

45:17.923 --> 45:19.049
So what are you, a hit woman?

45:19.133 --> 45:22.136
If I was, you'd be dead already,
but here we are, huh?

45:22.219 --> 45:24.805
You must have a lot of enemies
to ask something like that.

45:24.888 --> 45:26.598
Well, this is the world we live in now.

45:27.099 --> 45:28.016
If you want to survive,

45:28.100 --> 45:30.185
you gotta commit some crimes
just to get by.

45:30.686 --> 45:34.148
You can die for all sorts of reasons,
even if you're completely innocent.

45:40.696 --> 45:42.030
[Tae-sang sighs]

45:57.171 --> 45:58.172
[sighs]

45:59.006 --> 46:01.008
All right, now what is it you want?

46:01.091 --> 46:03.218
I heard you're
the information king of Gyeongseong.

46:03.302 --> 46:06.764
You must have heard my prices vary
depending on the information.

46:07.264 --> 46:08.265
The range is pretty wide,

46:08.348 --> 46:10.642
depending on whether
you need a high-level or low-level job.

46:10.726 --> 46:13.896
- It's all business, nothing personal.
- I am looking for someone.

46:14.521 --> 46:15.397
He's Japanese.

46:16.023 --> 46:17.733
- What's the man do?
- He's an artist.

46:18.317 --> 46:20.736
If they're not in the government
or in the service,

46:20.819 --> 46:22.780
they're pretty much low-level work.

46:22.863 --> 46:25.657
And, unfortunately for you,
I don't investigate anything that low.

46:26.366 --> 46:29.495
It takes too much of my resources,
and I barely make any money.

46:29.578 --> 46:30.996
The guy's name is Sachimoto.

46:31.705 --> 46:32.539
I don't know him.

46:32.623 --> 46:34.666
He looks to be in his mid-thirties,
so I've been told.

46:35.375 --> 46:36.251
Still don't know him.

46:36.335 --> 46:38.879
He also doesn't speak like
someone from here.

46:39.379 --> 46:41.131
So he must have come here
from Japan recently.

46:41.215 --> 46:42.841
And still, I don't know him.

46:51.058 --> 46:52.059
All right, I'll be honest.

46:52.142 --> 46:53.936
My mother's missing,
and I'm looking for her.

46:54.812 --> 46:56.271
She's been missing for ten years.

46:56.355 --> 46:57.439
Ah.

46:58.190 --> 46:59.274
Ah!

47:00.275 --> 47:01.443
So…

47:02.194 --> 47:04.279
so the man was her lover, this Sachimoto?

47:04.863 --> 47:05.697
What?

47:05.781 --> 47:08.784
To be gone ten years, whoa,
that's really quite a stretch.

47:08.867 --> 47:12.037
And what if she started a new family?
It'd be better not to look for him--

47:13.664 --> 47:14.998
You bastard.

47:16.542 --> 47:17.709
Just from the way you speak,

47:17.793 --> 47:20.504
there's no way
you are Gyeongseong's information king.

47:21.380 --> 47:23.131
If anything, you're the king of trash.

47:24.550 --> 47:25.509
[chuckles]

47:28.512 --> 47:31.932
Well… well, I won't deny that
'cause I agree with you.

47:33.183 --> 47:35.060
It's true, I was born trash.

47:35.143 --> 47:37.521
I had no choice but to live my life
fighting and clawing.

47:37.604 --> 47:38.730
I'm trash, indeed.

47:40.607 --> 47:42.109
Just watch your mouth, then.

47:43.402 --> 47:46.029
I wouldn't want to see you get killed
over something so trivial.

47:48.532 --> 47:50.200
You never told me your name.

47:59.376 --> 48:01.086
You've got beautiful eyes, you know that?

48:11.430 --> 48:12.848
I wouldn't push your luck, huh?

48:16.101 --> 48:18.812
I could reach over
and pluck your eyes right out, you hear?

48:22.608 --> 48:24.735
It was a pleasure
meeting you tonight, hmm?

48:26.320 --> 48:27.321
You're crazy.

48:28.780 --> 48:31.491
[pensive music playing]

48:34.703 --> 48:35.996
I hope to see you again.

48:42.753 --> 48:44.755
She wants to find Sachimoto.

48:46.798 --> 48:48.175
Who's Sachimoto?

49:09.571 --> 49:11.573
[pencil scribbling]

49:27.047 --> 49:28.548
[music stops]

49:28.632 --> 49:30.717
- [knocking at door]
- [door opens]

49:31.426 --> 49:33.762
[man] Mr. Sachimoto, you've been summoned.

49:45.732 --> 49:47.734
["Clair de lune" playing]

50:19.266 --> 50:22.436
What's the occasion, my friend?
You rarely pay me a visit.

50:25.772 --> 50:26.606
[sighs]

50:26.690 --> 50:29.109
So Myeong-ja's gone?
Do you know where she might be?

50:29.901 --> 50:32.863
Myeong-ja. Myeong-ja, Myeong…

50:32.946 --> 50:34.197
Ah!

50:35.532 --> 50:38.744
You mean that pretty courtesan woman
that I used to date?

50:39.703 --> 50:42.831
One time we were together,
and, well, she told me she loved me.

50:43.457 --> 50:45.459
[tuts] Then she got together
with Ishikawa,

50:45.542 --> 50:47.836
and… and she broke my damn heart.

50:47.919 --> 50:49.588
Why do you think I'd know where she is?

50:51.298 --> 50:53.216
It's been a week now
since anyone has seen her,

50:53.300 --> 50:54.634
and I thought you might know.

50:54.718 --> 50:57.054
Well, yeah, I have heard the rumors
that she had disappeared,

50:57.137 --> 50:58.263
but I don't know where.

51:01.183 --> 51:02.309
Why?

51:02.392 --> 51:04.519
Tell me you don't think I kidnapped her.
Come on.

51:04.603 --> 51:05.729
[scoffs]

51:08.023 --> 51:09.232
You're no help per usual.

51:10.442 --> 51:13.820
Oh, by the way, you should
spread your wealth a little bit.

51:13.904 --> 51:15.238
Help us out some.

51:15.906 --> 51:17.074
I heard the news.

51:17.783 --> 51:19.868
I heard you'll be losing
everything you built here.

51:19.951 --> 51:23.121
Ishikawa's gonna wipe you out,
so why not spend it on us?

51:23.914 --> 51:28.001
You get to be a patriot,
and the comrades gain a wealthy supporter.

51:31.171 --> 51:32.130
[chuckles]

51:34.549 --> 51:36.510
Well, I never go down without a fight.

51:37.469 --> 51:40.222
All I need to do is find Myeong-Ja,
then I'm in the clear.

51:40.305 --> 51:43.100
If she really could be found,
he would have found her already.

51:44.267 --> 51:47.479
He can't on his own, and that's why
he's got you wrapped up in his business,

51:47.562 --> 51:48.772
trying to drag you down.

51:51.149 --> 51:53.401
Yeah, but I'm sure you already knew that.

51:57.114 --> 51:59.991
[Tae-sang] You're really drunk.
Call it a night and go home.

52:00.784 --> 52:02.869
[man] They say in life
that you should work like a dog

52:02.953 --> 52:04.454
but spend like a saint!

52:09.918 --> 52:11.419
If you don't use your money

52:12.671 --> 52:15.340
to try and help the people
who could genuinely benefit from it,

52:17.008 --> 52:18.677
then what's the point in having it?

52:20.095 --> 52:22.347
Your obsession with all your money
has made you lose sight.

52:23.181 --> 52:26.059
I'll do with my money how I please.
You got that, Jun-taek?

52:26.560 --> 52:27.602
I might as well have fun.

52:27.686 --> 52:30.480
It's my money. I risked my life for it.
Do I make myself clear?

52:30.564 --> 52:32.816
You got no pride
in your homeland, is that it?

52:33.483 --> 52:35.569
There's no damn room
for Joseon in your small heart?

52:35.652 --> 52:38.238
Joseon has been oppressed by Japan
since we were kids.

52:38.905 --> 52:40.198
This is how we grew up, Jun-taek.

52:40.282 --> 52:42.742
I had no father in my life,
unlike you, who had both parents.

52:44.494 --> 52:46.830
Berate my character all you want.
I don't care.

52:47.664 --> 52:49.541
But don't ever insult my money again.

52:50.917 --> 52:54.546
I worked like an animal to get it.
This is the life I built. I earned it.

52:55.130 --> 52:58.175
I don't care what other people think,
nor your opinion of me.

52:58.258 --> 53:01.011
The money I've got locked inside my bank
has given me the power I need

53:01.094 --> 53:03.263
in order to survive in this world.
You got that?

53:20.197 --> 53:22.824
Ah, look who's still
out and about tonight.

53:22.908 --> 53:24.743
Do you mind giving me a ride home?

53:29.831 --> 53:30.790
[car door opens]

53:32.375 --> 53:33.543
[door closes]

53:36.338 --> 53:37.339
[knocking at door]

53:37.422 --> 53:38.381
What is it?

53:38.465 --> 53:40.008
[door opens, closes]

53:44.304 --> 53:46.139
Subject One has begun
showing some symptoms.

53:46.223 --> 53:48.350
[unsettling music playing]

53:51.436 --> 53:53.438
[watch ticking]

53:55.190 --> 53:56.775
Well, that was faster than usual.

53:56.858 --> 53:58.151
Will you come with me, sir?

53:58.235 --> 53:59.361
[sighs]

54:02.656 --> 54:04.324
[woman 1] Oh, please help me.

54:05.450 --> 54:07.077
Ah, my head!

54:08.787 --> 54:10.247
Someone help me!

54:11.957 --> 54:13.959
My head is hurting so much.

54:14.042 --> 54:15.252
[sobs]

54:15.335 --> 54:16.878
It hurts so much!

54:17.963 --> 54:19.089
She has the serum?

54:20.465 --> 54:21.549
No, only the Najin, sir.

54:21.633 --> 54:24.094
[screaming]

54:26.388 --> 54:27.639
[sobs]

54:30.976 --> 54:33.019
Then we have failed again.

54:33.103 --> 54:35.939
[crying]

54:38.191 --> 54:39.776
And what of our second subject?

54:41.152 --> 54:43.154
Subject Two has remained stable for now.

54:43.738 --> 54:46.825
What should we do?
Should we inject her with the serum?

54:48.827 --> 54:50.036
Proceed with her.

54:51.079 --> 54:51.997
Yes, sir.

54:55.625 --> 54:56.960
[door opens]

55:00.588 --> 55:01.548
[door closes]

55:01.631 --> 55:03.508
[unsettling music continues]

55:04.009 --> 55:04.926
[gasps]

55:06.469 --> 55:07.470
[retches]

55:09.014 --> 55:10.015
[groans]

55:11.308 --> 55:13.310
[bones cracking]

55:22.485 --> 55:23.445
Oh, you're back.

55:23.945 --> 55:26.072
Mrs. Nawol, you're still here?

55:26.156 --> 55:29.034
Actually, I have been
waiting for you, Master Jang.

55:29.117 --> 55:31.161
I talked to a broker earlier,

55:31.244 --> 55:33.913
and that's when he introduced me
to some sleuths.

55:33.997 --> 55:37.751
Apparently, they're expert detectives.
They know how to find missing people.

56:07.864 --> 56:11.534
So how exactly do you go about
your missing persons cases?

56:12.410 --> 56:14.287
Every situation is
a bit different, Master Jang.

56:14.371 --> 56:17.457
Even so, usually,
you have to have some sort of method.

56:17.999 --> 56:21.336
A secret approach that perhaps
only a few of your kind know.

56:21.419 --> 56:22.253
So what is it?

56:23.797 --> 56:25.590
[man] Our method is we don't give up.

56:26.132 --> 56:29.094
We track the individual persistently
until we find them,

56:29.177 --> 56:31.638
and we go to great lengths
to find where they are.

56:31.721 --> 56:33.681
We will not stop until they are found.

56:34.391 --> 56:35.308
[Tae-sang] Hmm.

56:36.559 --> 56:38.645
[tuts] So how many people have you found?

56:38.728 --> 56:41.272
If you think we're unreliable,
then find someone else.

56:43.274 --> 56:45.735
I'm entrusting you
with something very important.

56:45.819 --> 56:48.071
I'm just being thorough.
After all, I am the employer.

56:48.154 --> 56:48.988
It doesn't matter.

56:49.072 --> 56:51.116
The job's not worth enough
to put up with all this.

56:51.199 --> 56:54.869
[man] I would say we've had about
a little over 200 cases

56:54.953 --> 56:56.371
in the past ten years.

56:57.038 --> 56:58.415
Of those 200,

56:58.498 --> 57:02.335
we've found approximately 140 people,
including bodies of the deceased.

57:02.419 --> 57:04.671
[woman] You don't have to answer
every question.

57:04.754 --> 57:07.215
He's not the king of information
or anything.

57:08.007 --> 57:09.092
He's just the king of trash.

57:09.175 --> 57:10.468
[man] Chae-ok.

57:10.552 --> 57:12.220
I refuse to work for such a man.

57:12.303 --> 57:13.513
[whimsical music playing]

57:14.305 --> 57:16.099
What in the world did you do to her, huh?

57:17.600 --> 57:18.726
I did nothing, I swear.

57:19.978 --> 57:23.481
All I did was…
Well, I told her that she, uh,

57:24.399 --> 57:26.526
she had really beautiful eyes, that's all.

57:27.402 --> 57:29.737
- What?
- Let's go, Chae-ok.

57:31.865 --> 57:33.408
Don't you need to find Sachimoto?

57:35.285 --> 57:36.619
You said he is Japanese

57:37.328 --> 57:40.081
and that he's about 35 years old
and paints for a living, right?

57:41.082 --> 57:42.792
I thought you didn't deal
with low-level work

57:42.876 --> 57:44.461
because it isn't worth it to you.

57:46.671 --> 57:50.550
In principle, it is not,
but I believe this situation calls for it.

57:50.633 --> 57:53.094
So if the principle can change so easily,

57:53.178 --> 57:55.013
I guess it's really not worth much,
is it, then?

57:55.096 --> 57:58.558
Flexibility is necessary sometimes.
After all, I am a businessman.

57:58.641 --> 58:00.435
It's all about money with you, isn't it?

58:00.518 --> 58:01.895
I'm a desperate man, as well.

58:01.978 --> 58:03.897
I believe pathetic is the word
you're looking for.

58:03.980 --> 58:05.106
[chuckles]

58:06.357 --> 58:07.942
Here's how I'm useful to you.

58:09.152 --> 58:12.071
You need government connections,
Japanese officials,

58:12.155 --> 58:13.198
so you need my connections.

58:13.281 --> 58:14.949
Nobody knows more people than me.

58:15.033 --> 58:17.035
Government, politics, businesspeople…

58:17.827 --> 58:20.246
That's any time I want.
Anybody I wanna talk to.

58:20.330 --> 58:23.082
With that amount of people
working for you, Master Jang,

58:24.042 --> 58:26.085
you can find this Myeong-ja
all on your own, hmm?

58:26.169 --> 58:28.004
It shouldn't take too much of your time.

58:28.546 --> 58:29.923
If she's alive. She might be dead.

58:31.508 --> 58:33.801
Usually, if I pulled this many strings,

58:34.302 --> 58:37.305
a lead will surface
in just about a day or so, give or take.

58:38.723 --> 58:40.934
I haven't heard a thing so far,
so something's wrong.

58:41.017 --> 58:42.936
So you think she could've died already.

58:43.603 --> 58:45.605
Please find her,
no matter the state she's in.

58:45.688 --> 58:48.608
In turn, I'll ask around for Sachimoto.
I'll use all my sources for you.

58:48.691 --> 58:51.945
Don't do that.
We can handle our own business.

58:53.112 --> 58:55.240
Weren't you searching for your mother too?

58:59.410 --> 59:01.412
[emotional music playing]

59:02.705 --> 59:04.457
I'm sure I can be of help to you.

59:05.416 --> 59:06.459
In fact, I know I can.

59:08.169 --> 59:09.837
[man] Let me ask you something first.

59:12.882 --> 59:16.052
Are you a good guy or a bad one?
And please don't lie to me.

59:18.096 --> 59:18.930
[scoffs]

59:24.769 --> 59:25.895
I would say…

59:28.356 --> 59:30.858
that I am really serious
about surviving, no matter what.

59:37.991 --> 59:39.617
And how long do we have to find this girl?

59:40.868 --> 59:41.911
Father, wait.

59:44.163 --> 59:47.208
Till the cherry blossoms
lose their flowers.

59:49.294 --> 59:50.545
[music fades]

59:55.383 --> 59:57.385
[unsettling music playing]

01:00:11.899 --> 01:00:14.527
What do I draw today for you, sir?

01:00:14.611 --> 01:00:15.945
Go to the second cell.

01:00:16.029 --> 01:00:17.822
[pencil scribbling]

01:00:17.905 --> 01:00:20.617
You may step closer for a better look
if it's hard to see.

01:00:22.452 --> 01:00:25.622
Oh, just don't get too close to it.

01:00:27.498 --> 01:00:29.167
It could be dangerous for you.

01:00:31.002 --> 01:00:31.836
Yes, sir.

01:00:35.173 --> 01:00:37.175
[unsettling music continues]

01:00:58.738 --> 01:01:02.116
Uh, sir, is it okay
if I use a little light to see better?

01:01:03.326 --> 01:01:05.328
[music fades]

01:01:46.786 --> 01:01:49.080
- [screams]
- [creature roars]

01:01:49.163 --> 01:01:50.707
[upbeat instrumental music playing]

01:03:36.729 --> 01:03:38.147
[music fades]

01:03:38.231 --> 01:03:40.233
[soothing instrumental music playing]

01:05:15.578 --> 01:05:17.705
[music fades]
